CAT = "cscsWelfare"; SEG = "WEL"
Q = [
("Which of these must be provided as welfare facilities on a construction site?",
 "Toilets, washing and drinking water", ["A canteen serving hot meals daily", "Free parking for every worker on site", "A separate shower for each trade"],
 "CDM 2015 Schedule 2 requires toilets, washing facilities, drinking water, changing and storage for clothing, and rest facilities. A canteen with hot meals is not required."),
("What should washing facilities on site include?",
 "Warm running water, soap and drying", ["Cold water only, to save energy", "Hand sanitiser and paper towels only", "A bucket of clean water and soap"],
 "Washing facilities need running hot and cold, or warm, water, soap or other cleanser and a means of drying. Sanitiser alone does not remove cement or chemicals."),
("Why should you wash your hands before eating or smoking on site?",
 "To avoid swallowing harmful substances", ["To keep your hand tools clean and dry", "To stop your gloves wearing out early", "To cool down after heavy work outdoors"],
 "Lead, cement, oils and germs on your hands can be swallowed when you eat, drink or smoke. Wash first and use the rest area, not the work area."),
("A worker on site is clearly under the influence of drugs or alcohol. What should you do?",
 "Tell your supervisor", ["Let them carry on if they seem fine", "Send them home in their own car", "Cover for them until the end of shift"],
 "Someone impaired by drink or drugs is a danger to themselves and others. Report it to your supervisor so they can be removed from work safely."),
("You are taking prescribed medicine that may cause drowsiness. What should you do?",
 "Tell your supervisor before working", ["Stop taking it while you are at work", "Drink strong coffee to stay alert", "Say nothing, as it is private"],
 "Some medicines affect your ability to drive, operate plant or work at height. Your supervisor needs to know so your work can be adjusted; do not stop medicine without medical advice."),
("You find someone collapsed on site. What should you do first?",
 "Check it is safe and call for help", ["Move them to the welfare cabin", "Give them a drink of water first", "Leave them and finish your own task"],
 "Check for danger to yourself first, then raise the alarm and call the first aider. Do not move a casualty unless they are in immediate danger."),
("Where should you record an injury that happened at work?",
 "In the accident book", ["On the site noticeboard", "In the visitors' book", "On the delivery note"],
 "Injuries should be recorded in the accident book or the company's reporting system. It is a legal record and helps the employer decide if RIDDOR reporting is needed."),
("Who should you go to if you need first aid on site?",
 "The appointed first aider", ["Any worker with a first aid box", "The nearest pharmacy", "The client's representative"],
 "The induction tells you who the first aiders are and where the first aid kit is. They are trained to give first aid until professional help arrives."),
("What should you do when the fire alarm sounds on site?",
 "Stop work and go to the assembly point", ["Finish your task, then leave the site", "Collect your tools, then go outside", "Wait to see if it is only a fire drill"],
 "Stop work, make your equipment safe if it is quick to do so, and go straight to the assembly point by the nearest safe route. Do not collect belongings."),
("Why must you not leave the assembly point without permission after an evacuation?",
 "Rescuers may go back in to find you", ["Your pay may be stopped for the day", "The fire alarm may be set off again", "The site gates will be locked behind you"],
 "If you are missing from the roll call, people may risk their lives looking for you. Stay until you are told you can leave."),
("What is the best way to protect your skin from the sun when working outside in summer?",
 "Cover up and use high factor sun cream", ["Work with your top off to keep cool", "Use sun cream only in the hottest hours", "Wear a dark vest and leave arms bare"],
 "Construction workers are at high risk of skin cancer. Keep your top on, use high factor sun cream, take breaks in the shade and drink water."),
("A workmate seems withdrawn and says they cannot cope. What is the best thing to do?",
 "Talk to them and point them to support", ["Tell them to toughen up and get on", "Report them for having a poor attitude", "Ignore it, as it is not your business"],
 "Construction has a high suicide rate. Listening and encouraging someone to talk to a mental health first aider, their GP or a helpline can make a real difference."),
("What should happen to wet clothing at the end of a shift?",
 "Dry it in the drying area", ["Leave it on the scaffold", "Keep wearing it home", "Hang it in the plant room"],
 "Sites must provide somewhere to change and to dry wet clothing. Working in wet clothes increases the risk of cold-related illness."),
("Why is drinking water important on site in hot weather?",
 "It helps prevent heat exhaustion", ["It improves your hearing", "It stops dust reaching your lungs", "It reduces skin irritation"],
 "Heavy work in heat causes sweating and dehydration, which can lead to heat exhaustion. Drink water regularly and take breaks in the shade."),
("What does a green sign with a white cross show?",
 "First aid", ["Fire exit", "Fire point", "Drinking water"],
 "Safe condition signs are green and white. A white cross on green marks first aid equipment or a first aid room."),
("Where should you eat your lunch on a construction site?",
 "In the rest area", ["At your workstation", "Inside the site vehicle", "In the materials store"],
 "Rest facilities give you a clean place to eat away from dust and chemicals. Eating at the workface risks swallowing harmful substances."),
("Why is tiredness a safety risk on site?",
 "It slows your reactions", ["It makes PPE less effective", "It increases noise levels", "It makes tools wear out"],
 "Fatigue reduces concentration and reaction time, which leads to errors with plant, tools and at height. Tell your supervisor if long hours are affecting you."),
("You have cut your hand on a sharp edge. Before starting work again, what should you do?",
 "Get it treated and covered", ["Wrap it in tape and carry on", "Wash it at the end of the day", "Put a glove on over it"],
 "Have the cut treated by the first aider and covered with a waterproof dressing. Open cuts can let in infections such as Weil's disease and chemicals such as cement."),
("A worker has a chemical splashed in their eye. What should be done first?",
 "Flush it with clean water", ["Rub the eye to clear it", "Cover the eye and wait for help", "Apply cream to the eye"],
 "Wash the eye with clean water or sterile eyewash for a long time, at least 10 minutes, and get medical help. Rubbing spreads the chemical."),
("Where should you be able to find details of the nearest hospital A&E?",
 "At induction or on the noticeboard", ["Only in the client's head office files", "On the side of the nearest skip", "In the plant operator's manual"],
 "Emergency arrangements, first aiders and the route to the nearest hospital are given at induction and displayed on site."),
("Why must welfare facilities be kept clean?",
 "To protect workers' health", ["To pass the client's audit only", "So visitors are impressed", "To reduce the electricity bill"],
 "Dirty welfare areas spread illness and infection. Report damaged or dirty facilities so they can be fixed."),
("What should you do if the drinking water on site looks or tastes contaminated?",
 "Stop using it and report it", ["Boil it in the kettle first", "Add squash to hide the taste", "Use it only for hot drinks"],
 "Contaminated water can cause illness. Stop using it, warn others and tell your supervisor so a safe supply can be arranged."),
("Who should you tell if you feel unwell at work?",
 "Your supervisor", ["Nobody until the break", "The site security guard", "The delivery driver"],
 "Feeling dizzy or sick can be dangerous on site, especially at height or near plant. Tell your supervisor so you can stop work safely and get help."),
("Why is it important to know where the site assembly point is?",
 "To reach it quickly in an emergency", ["To meet deliveries there each day", "To know where you are allowed to smoke", "To park your car as close as you can"],
 "In a fire or other emergency there is no time to look for it. The induction shows the assembly point and escape routes."),
]
